{
  "title": "The cache-aside pattern",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "narration": "Your database is the bottleneck. Here's the pattern almost every big app uses to fix it.",
      "data": {
        "kicker": "System design in 40 seconds",
        "title": "Why reads get 20× faster with a cache",
        "icons": ["api", "cache", "database"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "architecture",
      "heading": "Without a cache",
      "narration": "A request comes in. The API queries the database, and waits. Around forty milliseconds, every single time.",
      "data": {
        "nodes": [
          {"id": "client", "kind": "client", "label": "Client"},
          {"id": "api", "kind": "api", "label": "API"},
          {"id": "db", "kind": "database", "label": "Postgres"}
        ],
        "edges": [
          {"from": "client", "to": "api", "label": "HTTP"},
          {"from": "api", "to": "db", "label": "SQL"}
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {"at": "request", "action": "packet", "path": ["client", "api", "db"]},
        {"at": "waits", "action": "highlight", "target": "db", "hold": 2.2},
        {"at": "forty milliseconds", "action": "label", "target": "db", "text": "40 ms"},
        {"at": "every single", "action": "packet", "path": ["db", "api", "client"], "hop": 0.45}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "architecture",
      "heading": "Check the cache first",
      "narration": "So we put Redis in front of it. The API checks the cache first. On a hit, the answer comes straight back from memory.",
      "data": {
        "carry": true,
        "nodes": [
          {"id": "client", "kind": "client", "label": "Client"},
          {"id": "api", "kind": "api", "label": "API"},
          {"id": "cache", "kind": "cache", "label": "Redis"},
          {"id": "db", "kind": "database", "label": "Postgres"}
        ],
        "edges": [
          {"from": "client", "to": "api"},
          {"from": "api", "to": "cache"},
          {"from": "api", "to": "db"}
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {"at": "Redis", "action": "reveal", "target": "cache"},
        {"at": "checks", "action": "packet", "path": ["client", "api", "cache"], "hop": 0.45},
        {"at": "hit", "action": "highlight", "target": "cache", "tone": "ok", "hold": 2.4},
        {"at": "hit", "action": "label", "target": "cache", "text": "HIT", "tone": "ok"},
        {"at": "straight back", "action": "packet", "path": ["cache", "api", "client"], "tone": "ok", "hop": 0.4}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "architecture",
      "heading": "On a miss, fill it",
      "narration": "On a miss, the API reads the database, then writes the result into the cache, so the next request is fast.",
      "data": {
        "carry": true,
        "nodes": [
          {"id": "client", "kind": "client", "label": "Client"},
          {"id": "api", "kind": "api", "label": "API"},
          {"id": "cache", "kind": "cache", "label": "Redis"},
          {"id": "db", "kind": "database", "label": "Postgres"}
        ],
        "edges": [
          {"from": "client", "to": "api"},
          {"from": "api", "to": "cache"},
          {"from": "api", "to": "db"}
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {"at": "miss", "action": "fail", "target": "cache"},
        {"at": "miss", "action": "label", "target": "cache", "text": "MISS", "tone": "fail"},
        {"at": "reads", "action": "packet", "path": ["api", "db", "api"], "hop": 0.45},
        {"at": "writes", "action": "packet", "path": ["api", "cache"], "tone": "ok"},
        {"at": "writes", "action": "label", "target": "cache", "text": "STORED", "tone": "ok", "delay": 0.5},
        {"at": "next request", "action": "highlight", "target": "cache", "tone": "ok", "hold": 1.5}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "heading": "In code, it's six lines",
      "narration": "In code, you check the cache, fall back to the database on a miss, then store the result with an expiry.",
      "data": {
        "file": "users.py",
        "code": [
          "def get_user(user_id):",
          "    key = f\"user:{user_id}\"",
          "    if (cached := redis.get(key)):",
          "        return cached",
          "    user = db.fetch_user(user_id)",
          "    redis.set(key, user, ex=300)",
          "    return user"
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {"at": "check the cache", "action": "highlight", "lines": [3, 4]},
        {"at": "fall back", "action": "highlight", "lines": [5, 5]},
        {"at": "store", "action": "highlight", "lines": [6, 6]}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "heading": "Why it's worth it",
      "narration": "A read from memory takes about two milliseconds, instead of forty from the database.",
      "data": {
        "value": 2,
        "unit": "ms",
        "label": "typical read from an in-memory cache",
        "bars": [
          {"label": "Redis", "value": 2, "tone": "ok"},
          {"label": "Postgres", "value": 40, "tone": "ink2"}
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {"at": "instead", "action": "bars"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "takeaway",
      "heading": "The one catch",
      "narration": "The catch: cached data can go stale. So set an expiry that matches how fresh your data really needs to be.",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          {"text": "Cached data can go stale", "tone": "signal"},
          {"text": "Pick an expiry that matches how fresh the data must be", "tone": "ok"}
        ]
      },
      "steps": [
        {"at": "stale", "action": "reveal", "index": 0},
        {"at": "expiry", "action": "reveal", "index": 1}
      ]
    }
